{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he divided them in the midst</b> — to cut a covenant with him, to pass between these pieces. And it was also hinted to him that from these would come every animal and bird offering, for the young of the dove is בן יונה, and it says concerning it גוזל (young bird), because they were not sanctioned in that species except the young ones. And even though all young birds are called גוזלים, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 32:11), \"As an eagle stirs up her nest, flutters over her young (גוזליו),\" Abraham understood on his own the chosen species, or he offered a dove's young of his own will, and Scripture chose forever the species that the elder offered. And he knew that these would be the offerings, and for all the offerings they would divide the olah into pieces, and the shelamim into breast and thigh and fats, and the sin offering and the guilt offering for their fats." "<b>But the bird he did not divide</b> — he placed the turtledove and the young bird each opposite its fellow, for they too were included in the covenant, but he did not divide them in the midst, because for every bird offering it is stated, \"he shall not divide it\" (Leviticus 1:17). And in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 44:14): the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him that they divide in the bird olah but do not divide in the bird sin offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:39.058341788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}